United Kingdom in 60 Seconds · History in 60 Seconds series · Silkscreen Travel Poster style

Picture: drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Print engine engine/silk.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (MIT).
Landmarks (standing stones, a wall over crags with a milecastle, a stone keep, a round timber playhouse, a stone bridge with a coach,
a viaduct with a steam train and mills, a domed cathedral under searchlights, an observation wheel and a clock tower by a river)
are original stylised silhouettes drawn as simple paths, not traced from photographs. No logos, no flags, no maps or borders.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/):
  Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / Google Fonts
  Outfit — Rodrigo Fuenzalida / Google Fonts

Voice: Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george. Checked with faster-whisper (MIT), model base.en.

Music (original score, music/compose.py): church bells (additive partials), brass band, snare and drums, all synthesised in code. No samples.
Sound (mix.py): paper swish, stamps, steam engine chuffs and whistle, wind, rain, larks, hooves, river, crowd, siren, town hum: synthesised in code.
Mastering: FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL) via imageio-ffmpeg.

Facts and sources: FACTS.md.
